                            {
                                "target_word": "rag",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1308e8f-a8ab-3e0a-b737-36d24f8c53fe",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tattered clothes (clothing)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially",
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a6618d5-518c-48ed-9f80-e60613ddb060",
                                                "sense_id": "f1308e8f-a8ab-3e0a-b737-36d24f8c53fe",
                                                "text": "—What a pretty dress! —What, this old rag?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20f0ab39-a800-49c2-9fa7-0786754364ca",
                                                "sense_id": "f1308e8f-a8ab-3e0a-b737-36d24f8c53fe",
                                                "text": "It's semiformal. I can't show up dressed in rags!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d409212d-6e91-4c42-9c51-4987fbaafb84",
                                                "sense_id": "f1308e8f-a8ab-3e0a-b737-36d24f8c53fe",
                                                "text": "rags to riches"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bed2464-018f-4e28-bf8a-e83f38f2e46b",
                                                "sense_id": "f1308e8f-a8ab-3e0a-b737-36d24f8c53fe",
                                                "text": "And virtue, though in rags, will keep me warm."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eecc3bff-9232-351b-b1ec-9a970ee39e5c",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A piece of old cloth, especially one used for cleaning, patching, etc.; a tattered piece of cloth; a shred or tatter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73a46c69-f289-4bf1-a7ee-475db78759f2",
                                                "sense_id": "eecc3bff-9232-351b-b1ec-9a970ee39e5c",
                                                "text": "Cowls, hoods, and habits, with their wearers, toss'd, / And flutter'd into rags; then reliques, beads,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29a68086-f7b1-46ff-abf4-f697425b1c9c",
                                                "sense_id": "eecc3bff-9232-351b-b1ec-9a970ee39e5c",
                                                "text": "[…]even by the law of their own might and malice, not having otherwise any rag of legality to cover the shame of their cruelty."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "680f1f04-f511-3166-9441-7675ddc95ce9",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shabby, beggarly person; synonym of ragamuffin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a47e0fb4-05e2-4b2d-9877-6977993fbbc5",
                                                "sense_id": "680f1f04-f511-3166-9441-7675ddc95ce9",
                                                "text": "For upon the like Proclamation there, they all came in, both tag and rag"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6740adad-a18a-4029-9693-d44bd6026936",
                                                "sense_id": "680f1f04-f511-3166-9441-7675ddc95ce9",
                                                "text": "The other zealous rag is the compositor, / Who in an angle where the ants inhabit, / (The emblems of his labors) will sit curl'd"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dba3ed66-617c-4e6e-ae12-af0cdb311949",
                                                "sense_id": "680f1f04-f511-3166-9441-7675ddc95ce9",
                                                "text": "Nor will it be achieved by marching in the streets in leather, drag, chains, fish net over-flying-tits or any other get up. It will not be accomplished by hung-over bar rags, hustlers, shallow queens, or angry dykes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "660fd8f4-e2c0-3a38-89da-03a3e2e379bd",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ragged edge in metalworking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a0bbcc2-b1f4-3c2e-b00b-1a1521bdc70e",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sail, or any piece of canvas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c2b4cba-7c42-4d1b-9bee-383c32f8cd75",
                                                "sense_id": "8a0bbcc2-b1f4-3c2e-b00b-1a1521bdc70e",
                                                "text": "Our ship was a clipper, with every rag set, stunsails, sky-scrapers, and all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b05ff85b-dc1e-4efe-b775-c7181bc1f88a",
                                                "sense_id": "8a0bbcc2-b1f4-3c2e-b00b-1a1521bdc70e",
                                                "text": "\"'Oh yes, that's all very well, but we haven't done with it yet,' said the lad, 'we shall have it worse directly,' and he ordered them to furl every rag but the mizen.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aebc9526-7839-3461-a216-ef388e950139",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sanitary napkins, pads, or other materials used to absorb menstrual discharge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural",
                                            "singular",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95b560fc-a1ea-4fb1-8ba4-7509f998739b",
                                                "sense_id": "aebc9526-7839-3461-a216-ef388e950139",
                                                "text": "\"It's heaviest on the first day, which might be why it hurts so much. After that, it slows down and eventually stops, but you'll need the rags for about a week.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "82efe5d2-a33d-3179-8604-eccc13d57fea",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A newspaper or magazine, especially one whose journalism is considered to be of poor quality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0c2956d-a19d-4bc6-a315-a25393c0f650",
                                                "sense_id": "82efe5d2-a33d-3179-8604-eccc13d57fea",
                                                "text": "\"You must behave yourself, dear. Mr. Malone is a Pressman. He will have it all in his rag to-morrow, and sell an extra dozen among our neighbors.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08e33e8d-f5e9-3c7d-aa69-e3565c471571",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A poor, low-ranking kicker."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53e1ab83-8592-4d7f-8b6d-264e84504ce4",
                                                "sense_id": "08e33e8d-f5e9-3c7d-aa69-e3565c471571",
                                                "text": "I have ace-four on my hand. In other words, I have ace-rag."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c748ad68-1a82-3030-943a-49db86613313",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A curtain of various kinds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "019d2b95-fafc-350a-815e-b19f74f27bf5",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person suffering from exhaustion or lack of energy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c54fb1c5-3538-470a-b9a3-d9624062d5ef",
                                                "sense_id": "019d2b95-fafc-350a-815e-b19f74f27bf5",
                                                "text": "\"It took it out of me, though. I'm a rag this morning.\" \"They work you too hard, dear.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "18e2b717-43e6-33b8-81d2-396091f5e460",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A banknote."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fc092d2-cb6b-4b69-bf12-634497f4c0c6",
                                                "sense_id": "18e2b717-43e6-33b8-81d2-396091f5e460",
                                                "text": "What was he at, do you think? Counting bank-notes; he had bundles of them. […] Well, Guv'nor, he stood up by-and-by, and taking the bundles of rags, the big uns in one hand, tother ones in tother, he toddled out of the room; […] So I tucked my violin under my arm, and sallied out after the old budgy ragman, determined to ease him of his load at the very first lonesome corner I could track him to."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd72f5d7-ab4e-3f5f-bfe4-11b9a7c6fc52",
                                        "entry_id": "bff3f4e8-b632-364a-bb0c-6a84c377258f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An uneven vertical margin (of a block of type)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec577513-30ce-41f7-9dc5-9755918de6d1",
                                                "sense_id": "bd72f5d7-ab4e-3f5f-bfe4-11b9a7c6fc52",
                                                "text": "We always leave rag on article typeset for the web."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
